From 274f3753fe0ecb0601b4c45aa0212fbdb19fc4c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 07:13:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] Use RGB 60 FPS, IMU 200 Hz and 400p tunnel IR

oak_fps_bench showed the OAK LeonCSS saturating with RGB 70 + depth 30 +
IMU 400 Hz, dropping RGB frames and delaying IMU past the stabilizer
limit. Tunnel mode no longer forces RGB to 70, and the 30 Hz TCN sampling
grid gets a 4 ms tolerance so 60 FPS input keeps 33 ms intervals.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011Bx8VEHU9jDi6F1rtEfbms
---
 src/camera_driver/config/camera_config.yaml  | 13 +++++++++----
 src/camera_driver/src/camera_driver_node.cpp | 17 ++++++++++++-----
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/camera_driver/config/camera_config.yaml b/src/camera_driver/config/camera_config.yaml
index 9ce5b03..dbea606 100644
